It appears as though the ranger start level is considered arboreal,
thus any tree that is generated in place of a wall (which I believe is
true of the ones that make up the maze) passes the IS_TREE check in
rm.h.  Any square that IS_TREE(x,y) has a chance of creating killer
bees, dropping fruit, or most likely doing nothing.

A quick test in wizmode dislodged 2 oranges from a tree on the second
or third kick, which is rather funny considering the trees are
petrified (try applying an axe in their direction)!  Of course, this
makes the IS_TREE define in rm.h make more sense... if it's really a
tree, or if the level is arboreal and it's rock.  Either way, kicking
it can create fruit!  After 20-30 tries I was able to get 3 killer
bees out of a tree...

